Yleaf-derived Y-DNA analysis
==========================

src/wgsextract_cli/ydna/yleaf_native contains modified code derived from
Yleaf v4.1.6, https://github.com/genid/Yleaf, commit
c167c4e8951623a53c370e7c300a0cfc7f411b62.

Yleaf was developed at the Department of Genetic Identification, Erasmus MC
University Medical Centre Rotterdam, The Netherlands, by Arwin Ralf,
Diego Montiel Gonzalez, Kaiyin Zhong and Manfred Kayser. The prediction/tree
implementation credits Bram van Wersch; Yleaf.py credits Diego Montiel
Gonzalez and extensive modifications by Bram van Wersch.

The original source headers license these files under GNU GPL version 3 or
later. WGS Extract's modifications and distribution retain that license;
the complete GPL v3 text is in LICENSE. Per-file headers identify the source
files and modifications. Yleaf data is distributed separately, unmodified,
with upstream provenance and SHA-256 checksums in the yleaf-data release
manifest (release tags: yleaf-data-v<VERSION>).

Please cite:
Ralf A, Montiel González D, Zhong K, Kayser M. Yleaf: Software for Human
Y-Chromosomal Haplogroup Inference from Next-Generation Sequencing Data.
Molecular Biology and Evolution 35(5):1291-1294 (2018).
https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msy032

The native adapter replaces Yleaf's CLI, process globals and pandas tables
with a typed library interface, existing samtools/bcftools integration,
verified lazy data downloads, deterministic marker presentation and result
provenance. Prediction rules and marker/QC filtering derive from upstream.
These modifications were made by WGS Extract contributors on 2026-11-01.
This project is independent and is not endorsed by the Yleaf authors.
